The diff adds plural `*_ids` handling in `app/assets/javascripts/discourse/models/store.js.es6`:

```js
if (m[2]) {
  const hydrated = obj[k].map(function(id) {
    return self._lookupSubType(subType, type, id, root);
  });
  obj[self.pluralize(subType)] = hydrated || [];
  delete obj[k];
}
```

This clearly performs one `_lookupSubType(...)` call per id. If `_lookupSubType` does a linear search over the side-loaded arrays in `root` (as the finding assumes), that would indeed create O(ids × side-loaded records) hydration cost. The diff itself doesn’t show `_lookupSubType`’s implementation, so the exact complexity claim ("linearly scans") can’t be proven here, but the review concern about potential performance/scalability due to per-id lookups is grounded in the new code path and is not a functional correctness defect by itself.
